      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. Let me analyze what needs improvement:\n\n1. The test class contains many unused data provider methods — only `data_plus` is used by the actual test\n2. Many unused imports\n3. The parameter naming in `test_minus_TemporalUnit` is confusing: `expectedYear/Month/Dom` are positions 0-2 from `data_plus` (the \"start\" date in that data), while `year/month/dom` are positions 5-7 (the \"result\" date) — but for the minus test the roles are reversed\n\nLet me write a focused, cleaner version:Now I'll run the compile check:The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused data providers and imports, reformats `data_plus` with one readable row per line, renames the confusing parameters (`year/month/dom` → `endYear/endMonth/endDay`, `expectedYear/Month/Dom` → `startYear/startMonth/startDay`) to clearly reflect the minus-test's perspective, and adds brief comments explaining the plus/minus symmetry being verified."
    }
